# Pairs with ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted in ReplicationReBootstrap. An entry s logged before its lineage was
# re-stamped can arrive after r aligned with the new lineage. Applied, it is a
# source entry the new contents lack, and the reconcile fabricates its delete.
# Reproduces production before #4681 (#4673): a batch carried no source lineage.
MODULE: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeletedStaleLineageApplied
TARGET: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an aligned receiver applies an entry the source logged under its old lineage, which a later pass then reconciles as a delete
PERTURBS: Deliver

--- FIND
       IN IF StaleLineage(e) THEN UNCHANGED <<reg, clk>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no lineage check on delivery.
       IN IF FALSE THEN UNCHANGED <<reg, clk>>
--- END
